AWS SageMaker Instance Types and Their Use Cases

| Type         | Main Strength      | Example Use             |
| ------------ | ------------------ | ----------------------- |
| **t3**       | Basic, lightweight | Learning Python/Jupyter |
| **m5**       | Balanced CPU + RAM | General ML              |
| **c5**       | High CPU           | Heavy calculations      |
| **r5**       | High RAM           | Large datasets          |
| **g5**       | GPU                | Deep Learning / AI      |
| **p-series** | Powerful GPU       | Advanced AI training    |


====

AWS SageMaker and running JupyterLab, start with:

ml.t3.medium
2 vCPU
4 GiB RAM

It is enough for learning:

✅ Python
✅ Pandas
✅ NumPy
✅ Basic Machine Learning
✅ Small datasets
✅ Jupyter Notebooks



====


⚠️ Always stop the SageMaker Space/instance after finishing, because running cloud compute can generate charges.

Simple formula to remember:

Instance = Cloud Computer
Instance Type = Configuration of that Cloud Computer
vCPU = Processing Power
RAM = Working Memory
GPU = Fast parallel processing for AI/Deep Learning

